A||N||2||87ProudGT||87 GT Engine Blower Motor||||9||
Z||000000||87ProudGT||09-10-2001||10:40 PM||||Last week my Alternator gave out, diodes open, replaced it with a rebuild. Works great, has a higher amp output, and I was happy. Yesterday, old reliable wouldn't start, no spark, Primary on Ignition Coil metered open. New Coil works great, and I was happy once again. <BR>Just another one of those strange things with Fiero's, but problems always happen in 3's when I've had trouble before, and I'm sure I'm not the only one to experience this.<BR>Last week I could hear strange sounds from engine compartment when driving, almost like a belt slipping, both alternator-A/C belts replaced with the  Alternator and retightened after Ignition Coil with no change. Got much worse today, took me a while to find noise is coming from the right side of the rear luggage compartment, sounds like a bearing going, fan grinding, or a cat is stuck inside. Very little, if any air coming out of the cooling tubes when it should. Somewhere inside is the Engine Blower Motor/Fan. <BR>There is nothing about this in my trusty Haynes Repair Manual. Searching the Forum, there are pros/cons about having one at all since the '88 didn't. I think every little bit of cooling helps and this might be a good example. <BR>What's the best way to get the blower out, back together, and working again?||||reg||9
Z||000001||72vinman||09-10-2001||10:45 PM||||The blower is located on the ride side of the trunk compartment. Just pull back the carpet and you should see it.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Leadfoot||09-10-2001||11:21 PM||||I read a similar thread about a week ago and quickly turned to my fiero manuals.  Of the 3 (haynes, chilton and helms) only haynes and helms mention them.  Unfortunately the do not describe where the motor is located.  You can find the electrical wiring schematics on p. 8A-37-1 in the 85 helms manual and p. 273 in the haynes manual.  If it wasn't for this forum I would have never known such a device existed on my 85.||||reg||1
